# Line endings are pinned here, not left to the machine.
#
# core.autocrlf is enabled system-wide on the Windows workstation this repo is
# developed on, and there was no .gitattributes, so every commit printed "LF
# will be replaced by CRLF" and a fresh clone checked text files out with CRLF
# while CI (ubuntu) checked the same bytes out with LF. Verified by cloning to
# a temporary directory: `git ls-files --eol` reported `i/lf w/crlf` there,
# against `w/lf` in this older checkout, which merely predates the change.
#
# That matters from FW6 on, because lib/ui/core/styles/_zones.scss is
# GENERATED and compared BYTE FOR BYTE against the generator's output. An EOL
# that varies by machine would make that comparison fail on a fresh Windows
# clone and pass in CI - and the reflexive fix, normalising line endings
# before comparing, permanently blinds the check to the EOL-only and
# trailing-newline-only edits it exists to catch. Pinning LF lets the
# comparison stay exact, which is the only form that detects every hand edit.
#
# The generator writes "\n" and never os.EOL, for the same reason.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces: text=auto already detects these as binary, but naming them
# means a corrupted heuristic cannot mangle an image.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pmtiles binary
